WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.863
Welcome to Crypto Market Decoder.

2
00:00:02.863 --> 00:00:07.374
In the next two minutes you will see what a blockchain records,

3
00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:13.605
why old entries are hard to change, and how to read crypto prices without being misled.

4
00:00:15.005 --> 00:00:24.131
A blockchain is a ledger of transactions that thousands of independent computers keep copies of and check against the same rules.

5
00:00:24.131 --> 00:00:30.427
New transactions are grouped into blocks, and each block stores the fingerprint, or hash,

6
00:00:30.427 --> 00:00:32.054
of the block before it.

7
00:00:33.454 --> 00:00:37.896
Each block built on top of a transaction adds a confirmation.

8
00:00:37.896 --> 00:00:43.867
A transaction in block one hundred, with the newest block at one hundred and five,

9
00:00:43.867 --> 00:00:45.469
has six confirmations.

10
00:00:45.469 --> 00:00:51.513
Reversing it would mean redoing all six blocks faster than the rest of the network.

11
00:00:52.913 --> 00:00:55.100
A wallet does not hold coins.

12
00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:58.492
It holds private keys that sign transactions.

13
00:00:58.492 --> 00:01:02.036
You can share an address so others can pay you,

14
00:01:02.036 --> 00:01:06.936
but a seed phrase or private key gives full control of the funds,

15
00:01:06.936 --> 00:01:10.178
and nobody legitimate will ever ask for it.

16
00:01:11.578 --> 00:01:13.158
Prices need care too.

17
00:01:13.158 --> 00:01:17.072
Each exchange runs its own order book for each pair,

18
00:01:17.072 --> 00:01:24.672
so bitcoin against USDT on one venue and bitcoin against US dollars on another are different markets.

19
00:01:24.672 --> 00:01:29.714
A reference price from a data provider is an average across venues,

20
00:01:29.714 --> 00:01:32.122
not a price anyone can trade at.

21
00:01:33.522 --> 00:01:37.900
Market capitalisation multiplies price by circulating supply.

22
00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:47.660
A hypothetical coin at fifty thousand dollars with twenty million coins circulating has a market capitalisation of one trillion dollars.

23
00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:50.818
With a maximum supply of twenty-one million,

24
00:01:50.818 --> 00:01:54.837
its fully diluted value is one point zero five trillion.

25
00:01:56.237 --> 00:02:02.963
In the course you will follow transactions in three dimensions, sign with toy keys,

26
00:02:02.963 --> 00:02:07.583
walk an order book, and read real, sourced data in ATLAS.

27
00:02:07.583 --> 00:02:11.797
Crypto is volatile and transfers cannot be reversed.

28
00:02:11.797 --> 00:02:15.687
This course is education, not investment advice.

